This package repackages dsh-vision-toolkit by Anionex, used under the MIT
License. The original project lives at:

    https://github.com/Anionex/dsh-vision-toolkit

and itself integrates agent-vision-toolkit:

    https://github.com/Anionex/agent-vision-toolkit

Upstream's build needs its full toolchain (a Python bootstrap, an upstream
manifest check, a skill verification, and three tsc passes), so upstream/ holds
its PUBLISHED output and scripts/build.mjs adapts it. Nothing about its
behaviour is modified; all three adaptations are packaging concerns:

  - `saxes`, `tar`, and `undici` are inlined into the host half. Upstream
    imports them as runtime dependencies its own installer npm-installs into
    the profile. This repository's installer only copies files, and the harness
    profile provides none of the three, so an as-is copy fails to load.

  - The browser bundle's `__ModuleLoader__` id is rewritten from
    "@anionex/dsh-vision-toolkit" to "@dsh-pro/vision-toolkit", because the web
    boot manifest looks a bundle up by the installed package name.

  - Only the payload the code actually reads at runtime is vendored — the skill,
    the pinned upstream snapshot, the Python worker, the requirements lock, and
    the patches. Upstream's README screenshots (roughly 4 MB) are not.

`package.json`'s `dsh.visionToolkit` block is preserved verbatim, because the
host half reads it back at load time to verify its pinned upstream checkout.

